  "id": "NSWG-COR-9",
  "summary": "Always triggering a configuration file load attempt from `OPENSSL_CONF` or the\ndefault location for the current platform may allow an attacker to load\ncompromised OpenSSL configuration into a Node.js process if they are able to\nplace a file in a default location.\n\n",
